    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 05/02/2007, the erection of a single storey detached outbuilding in two parts, the first measuring 5.0m in length, 6.5 in depth, and 4m in height, and the other part measuring 5.90m in length, 5.50m in depth and 4m in height was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class E of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the development is over 5m from the main house, and does not bring developments on site over 50% of the garden space.\r\n"
